  "description": "ENOYAI crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: 2(C118 H194 Ce6 Mn8 N4 O51 2+),C50 H92 Ce6 N4 O34 2-,H2 Ce1 N5 O16 2-,21(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce7 (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce9 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce7A (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce8A (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce9A (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce10 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce10A (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 39 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 0.840-3.906 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 18.88-135.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula 2(C118H194Ce6Mn8N4O51)·C50H92Ce6N4O34·H2CeN5O16·21MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 5 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV), Mn(III), Ce(IV), Ce(III).",
